# -- Test run artifacts
results/
allure-results/
# docs/blazeup/tools/BE/ holds tool OUTPUT, not source: one dated file per run of
# be_coverage / be_drift / be_unit_audit / be_test_blame, plus the raw jest json. Nothing
# reads this folder, every file is re-derivable by running the tool again, and four new ones
# appear on every pass — so they are local history, not repo content.
#
# Ignore the directory and re-admit only the two hand-written READMEs. Written this way round
# rather than as a timestamp glob so a tool added later is covered without touching this file.
docs/blazeup/tools/BE/*
!docs/blazeup/tools/BE/README.md
!docs/blazeup/tools/BE/README_vi.md

# Working notes for the in-flight "which endpoints has nobody automated" pass — a coverage
# analysis, a build checklist and a TC draft. They overlap each other on purpose while the
# work is live and are meant to be consolidated (and mostly deleted) once the TCs land, so
# they would only go stale in the repo. Local-only until then.
docs/blazeup/BE_COVERAGE_ACTION_PLAN.md
docs/blazeup/ENDPOINT_BUILD_LIST.md
docs/blazeup/NEW_TC_PROPOSAL.md
allure-report/
allure_report_test/
playwright-report/
.playwright/

